{"id":"HKF-088","kind":"appraisal","key":"D01","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"YES: Defines multi-UAV-to-edge inference offloading model (latency, energy, accuracy, connection duration) and distributed auction framework (UAV buyers, edge server sellers) in Sections 3-4.","evidence":[{"page":5,"section":"3.1. Inference offloading model","quote":"we design a collaborative inference architecture for UAVs."}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-088","kind":"appraisal","key":"D02","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"PARTIAL: States connection-time, capacity, and binary/single-server constraints (C1-C4) plus full-offloading assumptions, but omits Section 3.1 energy budget E_n^max from Problem P (Eq. 10) and ignores local compute energy.","evidence":[{"page":8,"section":"3.4. Problem formulation","quote":"the optimization problem is subject to a set"},{"page":7,"section":"3.2. Inference delay and energy consumption model","quote":"only the energy expenditure associated with"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-088","kind":"appraisal","key":"D03","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"PARTIAL: Reports 2x2 km area, node counts, task cycles/sizes, 5G NR radio params, ResNet-18/CIFAR-10, and 1,000 steps, but has server-count/frequency contradictions (5-10 default 3; 1-5 GHz vs 800-1500 MHz) and omits mobility trajectory, local CPU, and auction parameters.","evidence":[{"page":19,"section":"6.1. Simulation settings","quote":"The simulation area is a 2 2 km"}],"note":"PDFKit renders noise power spectral density as 10¼ W=Hz on p. 19."}
{"id":"HKF-088","kind":"appraisal","key":"D04","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"PARTIAL: Compares DADAO against Local-only, MWBS, LADPO, and OATS across CPU frequencies, node scales, and speeds, but omits baseline tuning/implementation details and does not evaluate energy consumption despite claiming energy gains.","evidence":[{"page":19,"section":"6.1. Simulation settings","quote":"We conduct a comparative evaluation between the proposed"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-088","kind":"appraisal","key":"D05","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"PARTIAL: Evaluates latency, accuracy, task success rate, and bidder/seller truthfulness matching Problem P and auction utility, but omits energy metrics and never explains how ResNet-18 accuracy varies with edge CPU frequency or offloading choice.","evidence":[{"page":20,"section":"6.2. Comparison of inference latency and accuracy","quote":"Figure 2 presents the performance comparison of"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-088","kind":"appraisal","key":"D06","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"PARTIAL: Sweeps edge CPU frequency (800-1500 MHz), node scale ([20,5] to [40,13]), and UAV speed (3-13 m/s) over 1,000 steps, but reports no multi-seed repetitions, confidence intervals, or variance statistics.","evidence":[{"page":19,"section":"6.1. Simulation settings","quote":"The total number of simulation steps is set"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-088","kind":"appraisal","key":"D07","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"PARTIAL: Models Shannon uplink rate, 200 m fixed coverage radius, speed-based remaining connection time (3-13 m/s), and retry/local fallback, but uses static channel gain (10) and omits fading, interference, packet loss, and trajectory dynamics.","evidence":[{"page":19,"section":"6.1. Simulation settings","quote":"The communication coverage radius of each edge server"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-088","kind":"appraisal","key":"D08","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"PARTIAL: Section 6 supports latency, accuracy, and success-rate gains in simulation, but Section 7 claims up to 45% latency reduction without matching Section 6 figures (19 vs 29 ms is ~34.5%; 13 vs 16 ms is ~18.8%) and Section 1 claims unevaluated energy gains.","evidence":[{"page":23,"section":"7. Conclusion","quote":"with inference latency reduced by up to 45%."}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-088","kind":"appraisal","key":"D09","status":"NOT_REPORTED","finding":"NOT_REPORTED: Checked Sections 1, 6.1, 7, ORCID, and References; no author code repository, simulation scripts, or custom dataset links are provided (only standard CIFAR-10 and ResNet-18 are named).","evidence":[{"page":19,"section":"6.1. Simulation settings","quote":"we construct a simulation platform that integrates ground"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-088","kind":"appraisal","key":"D10","status":"NOT_REPORTED","finding":"NOT_REPORTED: Checked Page 1 title/author matter and Page 23 Section 7 and ORCID; no limitations section, funding statement, competing interest declaration, or data availability statement is printed.","evidence":[{"page":23,"section":"7. Conclusion","quote":"In this study, we proposed a UAV inference"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-088","kind":"outcome","key":"Q01","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Metric: inference classification accuracy; literal: 91.5%; unit: %; method: DADAO (US); comparator: MWBS (89.6%); conditions: edge server CPU frequency at 1500 MHz (sweep 800-1500 MHz, ResNet-18 on CIFAR-10).","evidence":[{"page":20,"section":"6.2. Comparison of inference latency and accuracy, Fig. 2(a)","quote":"reaching 91.5% at 1500 MHz, outperforming MWBS (89.6%),"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-088","kind":"outcome","key":"Q02","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Metric: inference latency; literal: 19 ms; unit: ms; method: DADAO; comparator: MWBS (29 ms); conditions: edge server CPU frequency at 1500 MHz (sweep 800-1500 MHz).","evidence":[{"page":20,"section":"6.2. Comparison of inference latency and accuracy, Fig. 2(b)","quote":"with only 19 ms at 1500 MHz, compared"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-088","kind":"outcome","key":"Q03","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Metric: task success rate; literal: approximately 0.89; unit: proportion (0-1); method: DADAO (US); comparators: MWBS (around 0.84) and OATS (around 0.86); conditions: high-speed UAV mobility at 13 m/s (sweep 3-13 m/s).","evidence":[{"page":22,"section":"6.3. Performance evaluation in dynamic environments, Fig. 4","quote":"maintains a success rate of approximately 0.89,"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-088","kind":"report_coverage","key":"coverage","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"VERIFIED_EXACT: Checked Section 6 (pp. 19-23, Figs. 2-5) and Section 7 (p. 23); headline outcomes are printed verbatim in Sections 6.2-6.3 prose, while intermediate sweep points and Fig. 5 utility curves are plot-only.","evidence":[{"page":20,"section":"6.2. Comparison of inference latency and accuracy","quote":"reaching 91.5% at 1500 MHz, outperforming MWBS (89.6%),"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-088","kind":"technical","key":"t2_decisions_objective_solver","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Binary offloading a_{nm}(t) and continuous edge allocation f_m(t); minimizes weighted latency minus accuracy (Eq. 10) and maximizes buyer+seller utility (Eq. 15); constraints: connection time, capacity, binary/single-server; solver: O(MN log N) one-round uniform-price auction with bidder payment verification. Missing: objective weights, E_n^max in Eq. 10.","evidence":[{"page":9,"section":"3.4. Problem formulation","quote":"This optimization problem is a nonconvex"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-088","kind":"technical","key":"t2_partition","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Binary whole-task offloading without DNN layer partitioning: each UAV offloads its entire task to at most one edge server, with fallback to buffering or simplified local execution on failure. Missing: definition of simplified local execution and per-server accuracy model.","evidence":[{"page":9,"section":"3.4. Problem formulation","quote":"and (C4) guarantees that each task is assigned"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-088","kind":"technical","key":"t2_topology","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Two-tier UAV-edge architecture: 20-50 autonomous UAVs (default 25) as auction buyers and 5-10 fixed ground base-station edge servers (default 3) as sellers, coordinated decentrally without a central controller. Inter-UAV and cloud offloading are excluded.","evidence":[{"page":5,"section":"3.1. Inference offloading model","quote":"we design a collaborative inference architecture for UAVs."}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-088","kind":"technical","key":"t2_workload","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"ResNet-18 on CIFAR-10 (60,000 32x32 RGB images, 10,000 test); 1 task/UAV/slot (1,000-2,000M cycles, 3 MB input, 0.3 MB output). Baselines: Local-only, MWBS, LADPO, OATS. Missing: 3 MB vs 32x32 reconciliation and baseline hyperparameters.","evidence":[{"page":19,"section":"6.1. Simulation settings","quote":"we adopt ResNet-18 as the deep neural network"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-088","kind":"technical","key":"t3_network_event_response","status":"PARTIAL","finding":"5G NR sub-6 GHz Shannon uplink (1 MHz, 0.5 W, gain 10, 200 m radius), speeds 3-13 m/s, connection-time check dis/v_n, next-round higher-bid retry or local buffering/simplified fallback, and dishonest-seller exclusion. Missing: trajectory model, fading/interference, exact noise exponent (corrupted in text), retry limits.","evidence":[{"page":19,"section":"6.1. Simulation settings","quote":"The communication environment adopts the 5G NR"}],"note":"Noise power spectral density is garbled as 10¼ W=Hz in PDFKit text."}
{"id":"HKF-088","kind":"technical","key":"t3_platform_modality","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Pure discrete-time simulation (1 s step, 1,000 steps) over a 2x2 km urban area; no physical UAV hardware testbed or real flight traces. Missing: simulator software/language and host hardware specifications.","evidence":[{"page":19,"section":"6.1. Simulation settings","quote":"The simulation proceeds in discrete time steps,"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-127","kind":"appraisal","key":"D01","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"YES: Clearly defines multi-CNN stream collaborative inference across task UAVs (lightweight and complex models) and relay UAVs (complex model only) along links to a ground station, with communication, FIFO queuing, latency, memory, and accuracy models (Sections 3-4).","evidence":[{"page":3,"section":"3. System model","quote":"it is assumed that there are three CNN"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-127","kind":"appraisal","key":"D02","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"YES: Explicitly states UAV memory (Eq. 14), per-stream average accuracy (Eq. 15), full-layer coverage (Eq. 16), predetermined stable trajectories (Ref. 34), FIFO queuing, and negligible RL coordination overhead (28 Bytes vs 4,096 Bytes).","evidence":[{"page":5,"section":"3.3. Problem formulation","quote":"Our goal is to minimize the total latency"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-127","kind":"appraisal","key":"D03","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"PARTIAL: Reports embedded device profiles (Table 1), VGG16/AlexNet, bandwidths (0.5-2.0 MHz), horizons H=4-7, and swarm counts (3-4 task, 6 relay UAVs), but omits P_t, N_0, path-loss exponents, exact accuracy thresholds, MADDPG hyperparameters, and simulator software.","evidence":[{"page":8,"section":"5.1. Simulation settings","quote":"We employ VGG16 and AlexNet as the complex"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-127","kind":"appraisal","key":"D04","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"PARTIAL: Compares switching against Random-selection, Big-only, and GA (all using Algorithm 2) and partitioning against MCIA (PPO), DistInference, Average-partition, and Random-partition across tasks, links, bandwidth, memory, compute, and UAV counts, but omits baseline hyperparameters and achieved accuracy plots.","evidence":[{"page":8,"section":"5.1. Simulation settings","quote":"we introduce three benchmark algorithms, (A) Random-selection, (B)"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-127","kind":"appraisal","key":"D05","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"PARTIAL: Total latency and algorithm runtime directly match Problem (13) and Table 4 reports CV across horizons, but actual achieved top-5 accuracy per stream is never plotted or tabulated to verify Eq. (15) compliance.","evidence":[{"page":8,"section":"5.1. Simulation settings","quote":"the top-5 accuracy of the models is utilized"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-127","kind":"appraisal","key":"D06","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"PARTIAL: Conducts sensitivity analyses over task count (20-80), horizon H (4-7, CV in Table 4), bandwidth (0.5-2.0 MHz, Table 5), memory (128-1024 MB), compute capacity, and UAV count per link (Fig. 6), plus training curves (Fig. 4), but omits multi-seed error bars.","evidence":[{"page":9,"section":"5.2.1. Evaluation for model selection algorithm","quote":"we compared the performance and execution time of"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-127","kind":"appraisal","key":"D07","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"PARTIAL: Uses 3D air-to-air and air-to-ground Rayleigh/path-loss links (Eqs. 1-2), FIFO queuing at link intersections, and Mid-Air flight traces (Ref. 34), but assumes predetermined stable trajectories with fixed links, ignores interference/packet loss, and omits RL control latency via a 28-Byte estimate.","evidence":[{"page":3,"section":"3. System model","quote":"We assume that the UAV swarm adheres to"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-127","kind":"appraisal","key":"D08","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"YES: Conclusions align with simulated latency reductions under accuracy constraints and candidly note unaddressed extensions (diverse sensors, disparate task arrival intervals, pipelined execution) as future work.","evidence":[{"page":11,"section":"6. Conclusions","quote":"The simulation results demonstrate that our proposed approach"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-127","kind":"appraisal","key":"D09","status":"NOT_REPORTED","finding":"NOT_REPORTED: Checked Sections 5.1, 6, CRediT, Acknowledgements, and References; no author code repository, simulation scripts, or custom dataset links are provided (only third-party Mid-Air dataset Ref. 34 is cited).","evidence":[{"page":11,"section":"6. Conclusions","quote":"In this paper, we study the adaptive model"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-127","kind":"appraisal","key":"D10","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"YES: Reports future-work limitations in Section 6, CRediT authorship statement, explicit Declaration of Competing Interest (none), and three funding grants in Acknowledgements (p. 11).","evidence":[{"page":11,"section":"Declaration of Competing Interest","quote":"The authors declare that they have no known"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-127","kind":"outcome","key":"Q01","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Metric: coordination overhead estimate (analytical example); literal: about 3 2 2 4 28 Bytes (28 Bytes) and approximately 0.68%; units: Bytes and %; method: AMSM Task UAV 1; comparator: VGG16 smallest output layer (4 096 Bytes); conditions: Fig. 1 (3 relay UAVs, 2 other task UAVs, 4-Byte floats).","evidence":[{"page":7,"section":"4.3. AMSM algorithm","quote":"This is approximately 0.68% of the data generated"},{"page":7,"section":"4.3. AMSM algorithm","quote":"Thus, the total data required by Task UAV"}],"note":"Analytical calculation rather than measured simulation telemetry."}
{"id":"HKF-127","kind":"outcome","key":"Q02","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Metric: relative mean latency reduction; literals: 38.3% vs Big-only, 28.9% vs Random-selection, 8.3% vs GA (and approximately 25.2% average in Section 1); unit: %; method: AMSM (Algorithm 1); conditions: 20-80 tasks, all comparators using Algorithm 2 partitioning.","evidence":[{"page":8,"section":"5.2.1. Evaluation for model selection algorithm, Fig. 3","quote":"AMSM reduces latency by an average of 38.3%"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-127","kind":"report_coverage","key":"coverage","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"VERIFIED_EXACT: Checked Section 5.2 (pp. 8-11, Tables 2-5, Figs. 3-6) and Section 4.3 (p. 7); exact numeric tables (Tables 2-5) and prose percentage reductions are printed verbatim, while exact bar/curve values in Figs. 3-6 are plot-only.","evidence":[{"page":10,"section":"5.2.2. Evaluation for model partitioning algorithm","quote":"the AMSM algorithm achieved an average performance improvement"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-127","kind":"technical","key":"t2_decisions_objective_solver","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Decisions: binary model switching a_j^i and layer partition b_j^i; objective: minimize sum of per-task max latency across streams (Eq. 13); constraints: memory, per-stream accuracy, full layer coverage; solver: two-step AMSM (short-horizon enumeration Algorithm 1 + action-masked Gumbel-Softmax MADDPG Algorithm 2). Missing: MADDPG hyperparameters, radio constants.","evidence":[{"page":6,"section":"4. Algorithm design","quote":"we choose to address this problem in two"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-127","kind":"technical","key":"t2_partition","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Hybrid per-stream execution: lightweight model runs unpartitioned on task UAV with result relayed to ground station; complex model is sequentially layer-partitioned across task and relay UAVs along dedicated transmission links (FIFO queuing at intersections).","evidence":[{"page":3,"section":"3. System model","quote":"Each UAV along the communication link then sequentially"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-127","kind":"technical","key":"t2_topology","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Multi-UAV swarm of task UAVs S (sensors plus lightweight and complex CNNs) and relay UAVs W (complex CNN only) forming dedicated multi-hop links to a ground station G (simulated: 3-4 task UAVs, 6 relay UAVs).","evidence":[{"page":3,"section":"3. System model","quote":"The set of task UAV nodes is designate"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-127","kind":"technical","key":"t2_workload","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Multi-CNN streams using VGG16 (complex) and AlexNet (lightweight) with top-5 accuracy metric and Mid-Air trajectory traces (Ref. 34), 20-80 tasks. Baselines: Random-selection, Big-only, GA; MCIA, DistInference, Average-partition, Random-partition. Missing: image classification dataset and exact Acc_c/Acc_l/Acc_cons values.","evidence":[{"page":8,"section":"5.1. Simulation settings","quote":"We employ VGG16 and AlexNet as the complex"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-127","kind":"technical","key":"t3_network_event_response","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"3D air-to-air and air-to-ground Shannon links with CN(0,1) fading (Eqs. 1-2), bandwidth 0.5-2.0 MHz (Table 5), minor mobility on predetermined stable trajectories (Ref. 34), FIFO queuing at shared relays, and OOM failure noted at 128-256 MB RAM. Missing: link-failure recovery, interference, P_t/N_0/path-loss values.","evidence":[{"page":4,"section":"3.1. Communication model","quote":"Although the UAVs adhere to predetermined trajectories, they"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-127","kind":"technical","key":"t3_platform_modality","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Trace-driven simulation using real-world Mid-Air UAV trajectory traces (Ref. 34) parameterized with Raspberry Pi Zero, BeagleBone AI, Orange Pi Zero, and Raspberry Pi 3B+ specs (Table 1); no physical testbed. Missing: simulator/RL software stack and host hardware.","evidence":[{"page":8,"section":"5.1. Simulation settings","quote":"the task UAVs are equipped with Raspberry Pi"}],"note":""}
